# Currency Converter — Task 4

A simple Java HTTP server with a minimal HTML/CSS/JS frontend.
Real-time exchange rates are fetched from https://open.er-api.com (free, no API key required).

## Requirements
- Java 11 or higher (uses `com.sun.net.httpserver`)

## Build & Run

```bash
chmod +x build.sh
./build.sh
java -jar CurrencyConverter.jar
```

Then open **http://localhost:8080** in your browser.

## Project Structure
```
currency_converter/
├── build.sh
├── README.md
└── src/
    └── main/
        ├── java/com/currency/
        │   └── CurrencyServer.java      ← Java HTTP server + API handlers
        └── resources/web/
            ├── index.html               ← UI markup
            ├── style.css                ← Minimal styling
            └── app.js                   ← Fetch + convert logic
```

## Features
- **Currency Selection** — choose base and target from 39 currencies
- **Real-time Rates** — fetched live from open.er-api.com
- **Amount Input** — any numeric amount, press Enter or click Convert
- **Currency Conversion** — accurate result using live exchange rate
- **Display Result** — shows converted amount and the exchange rate used
- **Swap Button** — instantly swap base ↔ target currencies
